spec:
  grid_size: "10x12 to 22x22"
  colors:
    background: "most-common color (always 2/red [observed])"
    foreground: "exactly one non-bg color (always 4/yellow [observed])"
    output_added: "8/teal — replaces fg at '+' motifs"
  foreground_density: "26–41%"
  foreground_structure: |
    Mix of scattered small components (1–4 cells) and larger blobs/lines.
    Some components contain embedded '+' motifs (center + 4 ortho neighbors all fg).
    Plus motifs are NEVER isolated 5-cell crosses — always part of a larger connected
    component (size 6–61). Other fg shapes (non-plus) act as distractors.
  plus_motifs:
    count: "1–9 per grid"
    definition: "any fg cell whose 4 ortho neighbors are also fg"
    overlap: "none observed — plus footprints never share cells [observed]"
    min_L1_between_centers: ">=4"
    placement: "not on grid border row/col (centers need 1-cell margin)"
    embedded: "always attached to extra fg pixels beyond the 5-cell cross"
  transform_rule: |
    For every fg pixel (r,c) where all 4 ortho neighbors are also fg,
    recolor that cell and its 4 ortho neighbors to teal (8).
    Everything else unchanged. (Solver iterates interior cells only.)

generation_strategy: |
  1. Pick grid H,W in [10..22]. Pick bg (any color, e.g. 2) and fg (any other, e.g. 4).
  2. OUTPUT-FIRST: place K plus-motifs (K in 1..9) as 5-cell teal crosses on bg grid.
     Ensure centers >=2 from borders and L1-distance >=4 between centers.
  3. For each plus, extend 1+ arms by appending fg cells along an arm direction
     (so the plus is embedded in a larger component, not isolated).
     Mark the 5-cell cross as teal, extensions as fg.
  4. Sprinkle distractor fg shapes (singles, pairs, short lines, small blobs) that
     do NOT create any new '+' motif (i.e., no interior fg cell gets 4 fg ortho neighbors).
     Target overall fg density ~25–40%.
  5. DERIVE INPUT: copy the output grid, then replace all teal cells with fg.
  6. VALIDATE: assert main(input) == output.
